{
  "bridge_text": "The firefly's light flickers like a candle in a breeze, waiting for a gentle touch to steady her glow. With the heavy weight of the past shared, Mosk watches with a hopeful heart as Lina steps forward.",
  "resume_strategy": "continue",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "The firefly's light flickered, dim and fragile, as Mosk stood guard with his heavy heart. He had been her friend once, and the memory of that long-ago winter hung in the air like mist. Now, he watched with wide eyes, hoping that this time, he might finally make amends for the silence he had kept for so many years."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "The path ahead holds many secrets, and even the hum of the hollow tree has more to tell us as we step inside.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "text": "Inside the hollow tree she found a curl of stairs going down, and at the very top step sat an old grey fox in a patched green vest. His name was Mosk. He told her, in a voice like dry leaves, that the tree was not for visiting and that she should go home and forget the humming. Lina stood firm, her boots crunching on the wood, and told him she could not turn back when the music was only just beginning to call her name."
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "text": "Mosk pointed a clawed finger toward the door, his eyes narrowing. Lina reached into her pocket and pulled out the last apple of the season, setting it carefully on the step between them as a peace offering. Mosk stared at the bright red skin for a long time, his whiskers twitching. Finally, he stood up, adjusted his vest, and stepped onto the first stair, silently inviting her to follow him into the dark."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s2"
}

{
  "bridge_text": "Whether that apple builds a bridge or just a snack, Mosk has made his choice to lead the way. Down they go, into the heart of the hollow tree.",
  "resume_strategy": "skip",
  "replacement_segments": [
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "text": "At the bottom of the stairs, the humming deepened into a melody. A firefly the size of a robin lay upon a bed of moss, her golden light flickering like a dying candle. Mosk’s whiskers trembled as he looked at her. He whispered that she had been his friend once, but long ago he had failed to bring her the medicine she needed. Ever since that winter, he had guarded the tree in silence, too ashamed to look upon the friend he had let down."
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "text": "Lina knelt beside the moss, asking softly what the firefly queen required to shine once more. A drop of warm milk and a kind word were all the medicine the queen requested. Mosk hurried to fetch the milk in a tiny thimble, resting his paw gently beside the queen’s wing. As the firefly drank, her glow steadied and brightened. The humming within the tree transformed into a joyous song, and for the first time in years, Mosk hummed right along with her."
    }
  ],
  "active_scene_id": "s4"
}

{
